  "source": "Keyman Malay Jawi 1.0 by writingtradition (MIT). The number row types one set of digits (٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩): upstream mixes in ۰, ۴ and ۵, and repeats digits on Shift+4, 5 and 6, which type $, % and ^ here as on a US keyboard. K types ک and Shift+K types ك (swapped), the form Jawi dictionaries print. The quote key types ذ, the letter Malay uses, and AltGr+quote types upstream's ڎ; AltGr+A types آ and Shift+AltGr+A types أ, which upstream only composes from marks. Keys upstream leaves out keep their US characters.",
